Gegenprobe: ein Pin auf eine System-Wurzel gilt wieder über den Abgleich mit der mitgeschickten Wurzel, an der CT-Prüfung vorbei (Stand vor sec11 H6)
Modul: feature-login
Test: ch.brickinventoryapp.login.CertificatePinTest
Rot: a pin on a system root applies only with the system check, even if the server sends it along

diff --git a/Android-App/core-security/src/main/java/ch/brickinventoryapp/security/ServerTrust.kt b/Android-App/core-security/src/main/java/ch/brickinventoryapp/security/ServerTrust.kt
--- a/Android-App/core-security/src/main/java/ch/brickinventoryapp/security/ServerTrust.kt
+++ b/Android-App/core-security/src/main/java/ch/brickinventoryapp/security/ServerTrust.kt
@@ -274,7 +274,7 @@
         // A pin on a system root only counts via the system check including Certificate
         // Transparency: if the server sends the root along, the comparison would bypass the CT check.
         val publicPin = pin in systemRoots
-        if (!publicPin && fitsToPin(chain, pin)) return
+        if (fitsToPin(chain, pin)) return
         val situation = situation(chain, with)
         if (carriesPin(situation, pin, publicPin, fromCode)) return if (publicPin) checkSheet(chain[0], key, fromCode) else Unit
         val kind = if (fromCode) CertificateUnresolved.Kind.CODE_MISMATCH else CertificateUnresolved.Kind.CHANGED
